WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.516 --> 00:00:02.782
- He's an American
businessman and politician.

00:00:02.782 --> 00:00:06.449
- He has a net worth
of 250 million dollars.

00:00:07.572 --> 00:00:11.555
- He co-founded and led the
spinoff company Bain Capital.

00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:12.779
- He is Mitt Romney

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.839
and here are his top
ten rules for success.

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:18.784
(wind rushing)
(basketball bouncing)

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:22.497
- I believe having a clear
vision of where you want to go

00:00:22.497 --> 00:00:25.916
and being able to
articulate that to yourself.

00:00:25.916 --> 00:00:27.424
Perhaps writing it down.

00:00:27.424 --> 00:00:29.984
I take out the notes section of my iPad

00:00:29.984 --> 00:00:34.161
and will write down what
it is I want to accomplish

00:00:34.161 --> 00:00:37.220
and think about precisely
what I hope to accomplish

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.080
with a particular assignment,
so I'll write that down.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.614
So having a clear objective,
I think, is important.

00:00:42.614 --> 00:00:44.818
You hear the expression
all the time, you know,

00:00:44.818 --> 00:00:46.722
the grass is greener on the
other side of the fence,

00:00:46.722 --> 00:00:49.965
but don't forget, you can
only make the grass greener

00:00:49.965 --> 00:00:51.741
on your own side of the fence.

00:00:51.741 --> 00:00:55.220
You can't change the color
of the grass over there.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:59.440
You can only change the color
of the fence on your side.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.325
And so, the real issue is,
where is the best opportunity?

00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:06.090
Where can you find
opportunities in your life?

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.116
Where is an opportunity,

00:01:07.116 --> 00:01:09.663
for instance, to start a new business?

00:01:09.663 --> 00:01:13.746
I've met a lot of entrepreneurs
who started business

00:01:13.746 --> 00:01:15.866
and most folks think that
they're going to sit down

00:01:15.866 --> 00:01:19.713
in their study and think
and think and read magazines

00:01:19.713 --> 00:01:24.496
trying to find some
opportunity that'll allow them

00:01:24.496 --> 00:01:26.242
to become rich by starting a business.

00:01:26.242 --> 00:01:28.863
I haven't found a lot of people do that.

00:01:28.863 --> 00:01:30.993
Most of the people that I have found

00:01:30.993 --> 00:01:33.860
that were successful in
starting a business of their own

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.693
looked around them in
the job they already had

00:01:38.575 --> 00:01:41.741
and looked for opportunities
that weren't being filled

00:01:41.741 --> 00:01:43.960
by their current enterprise.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.131
Looked for customer needs
that weren't being met.

00:01:46.131 --> 00:01:46.964
Looked for something

00:01:46.964 --> 00:01:48.772
that just wasn't working
particularly well.

00:01:48.772 --> 00:01:51.572
Through all the occupations I've had

00:01:51.572 --> 00:01:56.319
I've experienced successes,
and as you know, failures.

00:01:56.319 --> 00:01:59.256
I'm asked what it felt like
to lose to President Obama.

00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:01.774
Not as good as winning.
(crowd chuckling)

00:02:01.774 --> 00:02:04.599
Failures aren't fun,
but they are inevitable.

00:02:04.599 --> 00:02:09.064
More importantly, failures
don't define who you are.

00:02:09.064 --> 00:02:13.397
Some people measure their life
by their secular successes.

00:02:13.397 --> 00:02:15.145
How high in the corporate ladder they got,

00:02:15.145 --> 00:02:17.282
how much money they made.

00:02:17.282 --> 00:02:20.237
Did they do better than
their high school classmates?

00:02:20.237 --> 00:02:22.011
If that's the kind of
success you're looking for,

00:02:22.011 --> 00:02:24.634
you're bound to be disappointed.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:27.571
Life has way too much
chance and serendipity

00:02:27.571 --> 00:02:29.878
to be assured fame or fortune.

00:02:29.878 --> 00:02:32.873
You need to have a life coach.

00:02:32.873 --> 00:02:35.472
You need to have someone
who'll tell you the truth.

00:02:35.472 --> 00:02:37.395
Tell you that the perfect
mate you've been looking for

00:02:37.395 --> 00:02:39.856
is no more perfect than you are.

00:02:39.856 --> 00:02:41.462
Tell you when you're wrong.

00:02:41.462 --> 00:02:44.251
Tell you what you need to
do to make things right.

00:02:44.251 --> 00:02:46.002
I can assure you that finding someone

00:02:46.002 --> 00:02:49.741
who cares enough about
you to tell you the truth

00:02:49.741 --> 00:02:53.161
and then is willing to take
time to give you their counsel

00:02:53.161 --> 00:02:55.786
and their coaching, that's invaluable.

00:02:55.786 --> 00:02:56.887
Look for it.

00:02:56.887 --> 00:02:59.324
My path in life has primarily been focused

00:02:59.324 --> 00:03:02.680
on doing things I thought
were fun and enjoyable.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.430
And so, that was fun.

00:03:06.271 --> 00:03:09.188
My undergraduate major was English.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.763
Everyone said, "Why would
you go into English,

00:03:11.763 --> 00:03:14.419
"I mean there's no future,
right, as an English major.

00:03:14.419 --> 00:03:15.706
"What are you going to do," right?

00:03:15.706 --> 00:03:19.425
But I liked reading and I
liked writing so I took English

00:03:19.425 --> 00:03:21.480
as my major and then coming
out of business school,

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.274
law school I went into
consulting 'cause I enjoyed it.

00:03:25.274 --> 00:03:27.346
Not because that's where I
thought I'd spend my life.

00:03:27.346 --> 00:03:29.609
I expected that I'd be there
for two or three years,

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.774
like most people do, and then get a job

00:03:31.774 --> 00:03:35.941
in a line corporation of
some kind and perhaps move up

00:03:37.676 --> 00:03:40.031
more aggressively by having
started in consulting.

00:03:40.031 --> 00:03:43.985
I loved consulting because I am oriented

00:03:43.985 --> 00:03:47.293
towards solving problems,
I like analysis and data

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.624
and problem solving and writing

00:03:48.624 --> 00:03:50.997
and writing presentations,
that's what I like to do.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:53.190
That's what took me there and so,

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:57.357
I would follow the career
path that you enjoy most

00:03:58.912 --> 00:04:01.599
as opposed to trying to follow
a career path that you think

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:06.202
will lead to the highest income
or the quickest promotion.

00:04:06.202 --> 00:04:10.903
Do what you enjoy and then
your life will be enjoyable

00:04:10.903 --> 00:04:12.000
and fulfilling.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.766
Now I'm going to draw a familiar account

00:04:13.766 --> 00:04:16.229
from the life of the
Savior to help me describe

00:04:16.229 --> 00:04:20.243
what I believe is the
secret to abundant living.

00:04:20.243 --> 00:04:22.320
You recall that Peter
and the other fishermen

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.981
had been unsuccessful in catching fish

00:04:24.981 --> 00:04:28.363
and the master directed them
to return to their boats

00:04:28.363 --> 00:04:31.239
to go out deeper and to
let down their nets again

00:04:31.239 --> 00:04:32.588
which they did and when they did so

00:04:32.588 --> 00:04:35.336
they were met with enormous success.

00:04:35.336 --> 00:04:38.278
These were the words that Luke records

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.389
that the master spoke, he said this,

00:04:41.389 --> 00:04:45.472
"Launch out into the deep
and let down your nets.

00:04:47.137 --> 00:04:51.304
"Launch out into the deep
and let down your nets."

00:04:52.797 --> 00:04:55.965
In some ways, these words
are a metaphor for life.

00:04:55.965 --> 00:04:59.130
Launch out into the deep,
don't live in the shallows.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:03.171
Live in the deep waters, grasp
every ennobling experience

00:05:03.171 --> 00:05:05.369
that's available to you.

00:05:05.369 --> 00:05:08.691
Embrace every dimension of
living that challenges you,

00:05:08.691 --> 00:05:11.757
that educates you, that elevates you.

00:05:11.757 --> 00:05:15.299
Live for purposes greater than yourself.

00:05:15.299 --> 00:05:18.759
Lose yourself in the service of others.

00:05:18.759 --> 00:05:22.790
Reach beyond the shallowness
of selfishness and complacency

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:26.462
and mindless conformity and of indulgence.

00:05:26.462 --> 00:05:30.483
This is the promise,
launch out into the deep

00:05:30.483 --> 00:05:32.394
and your nets will be filled.

00:05:32.394 --> 00:05:36.232
I did something to keep
things in perspective,

00:05:36.232 --> 00:05:38.651
to keep myself grounded.

00:05:38.651 --> 00:05:41.090
At the top of a sheet of
paper that was always placed

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.154
on the podium so we could
make notes during the debate,

00:05:44.154 --> 00:05:46.292
just before the debate kicked off

00:05:46.292 --> 00:05:49.042
I wrote at the top one word, dad.

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:53.577
I also drew a small image of the Sun

00:05:53.577 --> 00:05:56.070
and throughout the debate when
I glanced down at that paper

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:58.028
to look at my notes that I'd taken,

00:05:58.028 --> 00:06:00.827
I was reminded of my father's fearlessness

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:04.079
in fighting for what
he believed was right.

00:06:04.079 --> 00:06:06.552
And the Sun, that reminded me, of course,

00:06:06.552 --> 00:06:10.667
of that familiar scripture,
let your light so shine.

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:14.383
Win or lose that debate, I
hoped I would never do anything

00:06:14.383 --> 00:06:15.916
that would dishonor or discredit

00:06:15.916 --> 00:06:18.564
the things I hold most dear.

00:06:18.564 --> 00:06:22.639
Now during your life you're
going to encounter circumstances

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:25.008
that make you sweat.

00:06:25.008 --> 00:06:26.662
For many of you, the exams and tests

00:06:26.662 --> 00:06:28.816
won't be over when you graduate

00:06:28.816 --> 00:06:31.310
and you're all going to stand at podiums,

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.060
stand in front of a
boss to ask for a raise,

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.113
or work on some critical
project in your employment

00:06:37.113 --> 00:06:39.557
that'll make a big
difference in your life.

00:06:39.557 --> 00:06:43.724
At moments like those perspective
is a very powerful friend.

00:06:46.374 --> 00:06:50.894
You can welcome perspective
through preparatory prayer,

00:06:50.894 --> 00:06:53.097
by considering the
blessings of the temple,

00:06:53.097 --> 00:06:56.269
or by simply glancing at your CTR ring.

00:06:56.269 --> 00:07:00.331
Find ways to keep your
life in perspective.

00:07:00.331 --> 00:07:02.018
If you're spending all of your time

00:07:02.018 --> 00:07:04.034
in one aspect of your
life and not devoting it

00:07:04.034 --> 00:07:05.894
to other things that are important to you,

00:07:05.894 --> 00:07:08.569
then obviously things are out of whack.

00:07:08.569 --> 00:07:10.813
A couple of things I backed into.

00:07:10.813 --> 00:07:14.373
You're in the joint program,
business law program.

00:07:14.373 --> 00:07:17.109
I came from Brigham Young
University to Harvard

00:07:17.109 --> 00:07:20.269
and was convinced that I would flunk out.

00:07:20.269 --> 00:07:21.945
'Cause I looked around
and I saw all these people

00:07:21.945 --> 00:07:23.912
who were obviously smarter than me

00:07:23.912 --> 00:07:26.937
and how was I possibly going
to make it in this environment

00:07:26.937 --> 00:07:28.612
except by just studying like crazy,

00:07:28.612 --> 00:07:30.699
and so I studied all the time.

00:07:30.699 --> 00:07:33.883
And if I was not studying, I felt like

00:07:33.883 --> 00:07:35.645
there's this black cloud hanging over me.

00:07:35.645 --> 00:07:38.054
I should be studying,
I've got to be working,

00:07:38.054 --> 00:07:39.688
because I'm going to flunk out.

00:07:39.688 --> 00:07:43.276
And it was omnipresent, and
at some point I finally said,

00:07:43.276 --> 00:07:45.274
you know what, I'm going to do something

00:07:45.274 --> 00:07:47.899
which goes back to biblical times.

00:07:47.899 --> 00:07:50.549
I'm going take Sunday
off, I'm going to decide

00:07:50.549 --> 00:07:53.751
I'm not going to study at all on Sunday

00:07:53.751 --> 00:07:58.013
and I'm going to devote that
day to my family, to worship,

00:07:58.013 --> 00:08:02.291
and just personal time and
it was amazing what happened

00:08:02.291 --> 00:08:05.600
when I made that decision
because then on that Sunday

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.908
I didn't feel the black
cloud there anymore.

00:08:07.908 --> 00:08:10.535
It's like, OK, I can't study today.

00:08:10.535 --> 00:08:11.980
I don't have to worry about it.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:15.424
And the same thing happened
as I went into my career

00:08:15.424 --> 00:08:17.087
in the consulting industry.

00:08:17.087 --> 00:08:19.032
I said, you know what,
I'm just not going to work

00:08:19.032 --> 00:08:21.920
when I come home at the end of the day.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:22.908
It may be a late night,

00:08:22.908 --> 00:08:24.735
it may be I get home at
six or seven instead,

00:08:24.735 --> 00:08:27.436
but when I come home I'm
going to close my briefcase

00:08:27.436 --> 00:08:30.618
and not work, and I'm
going to devote the time

00:08:30.618 --> 00:08:34.005
I have at home to my family,
and it was wonderful.

00:08:34.005 --> 00:08:38.430
It was freeing, because
I could really focus

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.520
on the things that I
cared most about in life,

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.874
which were my wife and my kids.

00:08:42.874 --> 00:08:45.598
Your job will expand your skills,

00:08:45.598 --> 00:08:50.165
it will demand your ability,
your energy, and your time.

00:08:50.165 --> 00:08:52.332
Hard work, ennobling work.

00:08:53.806 --> 00:08:58.302
Dive into your profession
with passion and heart.

00:08:58.302 --> 00:09:01.068
Go beyond what's expected or required

00:09:01.068 --> 00:09:03.376
and in doing so, by
the way, you will learn

00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:05.727
the secret to advancement.

00:09:05.727 --> 00:09:08.978
And that is doing your present job well.

00:09:08.978 --> 00:09:12.645
Each of you here will
influence other lives.

00:09:13.633 --> 00:09:15.421
Think of that.

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:17.565
Perhaps you'll shape history.

00:09:17.565 --> 00:09:20.547
Perhaps you'll shape one person's history.

00:09:20.547 --> 00:09:24.853
Consider with care how
you act, what you say,

00:09:24.853 --> 00:09:27.124
and to what you're going
to devote your life to,

00:09:27.124 --> 00:09:30.126
because I assure you, your choices

00:09:30.126 --> 00:09:32.841
will shape the lives of other people.

00:09:32.841 --> 00:09:34.388
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:34.388 --> 00:09:37.683
I made this video because
iambergeson asked me to.

00:09:37.683 --> 00:09:38.946
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:09:38.946 --> 00:09:40.143
you want me to profile next,

00:09:40.143 --> 00:09:41.485
leave it in the comments below

00:09:41.485 --> 00:09:42.648
and I'll see what I can do.

00:09:42.648 --> 00:09:45.011
I'd also love to know
which of the 10 rules

00:09:45.011 --> 00:09:47.530
meant the most to you,
had the biggest impact.

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:49.851
Leave it in the comments, I'm
going to join in the discussion.

00:09:49.851 --> 00:09:51.292
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:51.292 --> 00:09:54.005
Continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

00:09:54.005 --> 00:09:56.702
(wind howling)
(basketball bouncing)

